00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:23,000
Summer has come again this year.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,980
It's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here!

5
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:28,580
[unintelligible]

6
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:34,440
[unintelligible]

7
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:35,800
Agisame

8
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:40,840
Summer has come again this year.

9
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:43,360
It's here, it's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here!

10
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,680
Summer has come again this year.

11
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,680
Clack! Clack! Clack! Clack! Clack!

12
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:49,260
That's odd.

13
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:51,340
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves.

14
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:52,200
Tiny haze ones.

15
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,160
Good for the southern breeze, too.

16
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:57,200
Big yosshiri, small yosshiri, tiny yosshiri.

17
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:58,260
Tiny haze ones.

18
00:00:58,260 --> 00:00:59,140
Akusa.

19
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:01,460
Buri buri buri buri buri buri buri.

20
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,720
Ah ah ah.

21
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,360
Good for the southern breeze, too.

22
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:11,000
Ah ah ah.

23
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,160
Blowing on the southern breeze.

24
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:20,520
On the shore, mud flies.
On the shore, mud flies.

25
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:37,700
Everyone, we're ordering lunch,

26
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,280
what'll you have?

27
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,520
Chashu noodles and gyoza.

28
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,580
I'll get the liver and
garlic chives stir-fry.

29
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:46,880
Then I'll have the fried rice.

30
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:48,080
What about you, Ryo-chan?

31
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:51,920
It's before payday,
so ramen and rice for me.

32
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,640
What are you doing, Ryo-chan?

33
00:01:58,300 --> 00:01:59,800
Don't tell me you're on a diet?

34
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:03,860
No way, not Ryo-chan.
That could never happen, right?

35
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:06,140
As if I'd ever go on a diet!

36
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:10,200
I'm working out hard like
this to build up my appetite.

37
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,020
So you're not hungry, then?

38
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,572
That's not it.

39
00:02:14,622 --> 00:02:17,620
There's a party at Nakagawa's place today,
remember?

40
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,640
That's right.

41
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,180
Hey, Nakagawa. Is there going to
be amazing food at tonight's party?

42
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:24,813
Yes.

43
00:02:24,863 --> 00:02:29,960
Chefs and sushi chefs of tetsujin caliber
are going to prepare it with all their skill.

44
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:32,920
Food like that is rare to get to eat,
you know.

45
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,760
So that's why you're starving yourself?

46
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,860
Of course. Not that I'm bragging.

47
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:39,920
I haven't eaten a thing since yesterday.

48
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:43,140
You can't work on an empty stomach, can you?

49
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:44,660
Shouldn't you at least eat lunch?

50
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:47,280
With all due respect, Chief,
even though you're my boss,

51
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,980
you have no right to order
what your subordinates eat.

52
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,880
Besides, chashu noodles with gyoza?

53
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,020
Is it really okay to
eat something so filling?

54
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,540
You won't be able to eat at the party,
you know.

55
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:00,180
Y-yeah, you're right.

56
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:02,700
Reiko, forget the gyoza.

57
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:05,120
Just get me the chashu noodles.

58
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:05,740
Yes.

59
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:09,400
I'll skip the liver and leek stir-fry too.
Just ramen for me.

60
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,265
Nakagawa,

61
00:03:23,315 --> 00:03:27,280
Party, party...
what kind of party is it, anyway?

62
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:30,480
It's the birthday party for the
prince of the Kingdom of Pondara.

63
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,080
Kingdom of Pondara?

64
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:34,860
It's a small country,
so I doubt you've heard of it,

65
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:38,360
but the king and my father have
been friends since long ago,

66
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:41,760
and whenever he visits Japan,
he always stays at our house.

67
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:52,220
This is the first time I've ever
ridden in a Ferrari this wide.

68
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:55,940
I asked the chairman of Ferrari
to make it a wide body for me.

69
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:59,540
But isn't this a lane-crossing violation?

70
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:03,340
It's fine, this is a private
road in Nakagawa Prefecture.

71
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,260
What?

72
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:04,360
So?

73
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:08,527
Back there, there was a sign that said
"Orita Interchange, Nakagawa Exit,"

74
00:04:08,577 --> 00:04:10,740
don't tell me the
"Naka" in Nakagawa is from you?

75
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:14,160
Yes. We had it built for our family.

76
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,880
Never mind that, are we still not there yet?

77
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:21,560
I'm so hungry I'm going to die.

78
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:24,280
No, we've already arrived.

79
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,284
What? I can't even see our house.

80
00:04:26,334 --> 00:04:28,780
All there is is a wall
that just keeps going.

81
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,460
My house is on the other side of that wall.

82
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:32,080
What?

83
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,640
How big is the grounds, exactly?

84
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,100
I bet it's a hundred times
bigger than Disneyland.

85
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,520
What?

86
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:03,500
If it's that big,
one front gate isn't enough,

87
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,000
you need gates all over the place,
don't you?

88
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,480
There are twelve gates in total.

89
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:11,160
The one closest to us right now

90
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:14,180
is called Mishima Kōmon,
and we're heading there.

91
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:15,700
Mishima Kōmon

92
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:18,040
There's also Daisen-mon,

93
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,340
Seishun-no-Mon,

94
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:21,440
Hinokuni-mon, Bunzai-mon, and others.

95
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,920
Make way, coming through!

96
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:43,860
Here we are, I'm going to speed up!

97
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,080
What's wrong?

98
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,700
Looks like we got lost.

99
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:01,040
Don't get lost on your own!

100
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,820
I'll start navigation right away.

101
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:06,020
Please confirm your destination.

102
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,840
We can't reach it on the
grounds without using navigation.

103
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:17,740
Finally, the house is in sight!

104
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:20,100
It's about the same size
as the chief's house.

105
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,740
For such a big estate,
it's pretty small, isn't it?

106
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:23,980
What?

107
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:27,180
It's a fine house, isn't it?

108
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:30,100
Sorry, that's actually a doghouse.

109
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:36,660
So the chief has been paying off a loan for twenty
years on a house that's the same as a doghouse?

110
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,500
R-Ryo-san...

111
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,400
Stop laughing so much.

112
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,340
W-what?!

113
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:57,640
A house... within a house?

114
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:01,500
Well, technically, it's a room.

115
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:05,180
My parents live in that
house you can see over there.

116
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:08,540
And beyond that is my sister's house.

117
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:13,280
It's a rather modest, humble little home.

118
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:15,760
Here, come in.

119
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:22,740
So this is the living room?

120
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,000
That's...

121
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,560
Wow, a classic Space Invaders game!

122
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:31,220
And it's the black-and-white
cellophane-covered version!

123
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:33,700
Amazing.

124
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:36,640
It even has a pool!

125
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:39,500
No, that's a bath, you know.

126
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,500
The pool is over here.

127
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,400
The bathroom started moving!

128
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:50,180
No, it's this entire room that's moving.

129
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:51,460
This room is...

130
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,080
Even the amusement park
pool is just for show

131
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,480
A golf course...

132
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:01,000
...even an airfield!

133
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:04,020
Yes! 50,000 points!

134
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:05,340
Did you see that?

135
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,600
Ryo-sama's knife-wear strike!

136
00:08:09,020 --> 00:08:10,600
Let's leave him alone.

137
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:16,980
What the...

138
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:30,580
What happened?

139
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,400
Is this all right?

140
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,540
Here you go.

141
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:03,500
Reiko, you look so lovely.

142
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:04,820
Thank you very much.

143
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:08,480
Having to dress up this stiffly...

144
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:13,700
We've invited celebrities from every field,
so please bear with it.

145
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:18,400
Still, Ryotsu,
you look no different even in a tuxedo.

146
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,260
That's none of your business.

147
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:25,260
W-what's this? An earthquake?

148
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:27,580
Everyone, stay calm!

149
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:33,560
As police officers, we must remain calm
and composed no matter the situation!

150
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,720
It's not an earthquake, Senpai.

151
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,600
This is an elevator.

152
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:42,740
What? This whole room is an elevator?

153
00:09:44,005 --> 00:09:47,940
So I live in a house
smaller than an elevator.

154
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:50,780
Welcome.

155
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:01,020
Wow, what a crowd.

156
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:04,140
Look, look!
Prime Minister Hashimoto is here too.

157
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:12,160
Over there are entertainers like Sara Takaoka,
who's always getting hurt, and Sabu Kitajima, whom the Chief likes.

158
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:15,520
Let's get their autographs later.

159
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,400
Ridiculous.

160
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,700
Never mind that, food, food!

161
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,720
Senpai, wait up.

162
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:23,920
What's your problem?

163
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:26,740
I'm about to introduce
you to Prince Hondara.

164
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,740
Hey, Prince Hondara.

165
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:33,700
Okay, Chief.

166
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:36,680
Happy birthday.

167
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:38,000
Thank you.

168
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:42,300
You called him a prince,
so I figured he'd be someone cooler...

169
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:44,620
but he's just a chubby brat.

170
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:46,080
Ryo-chan.

171
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:50,340
What?

172
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:58,620
Well, Prince, let me introduce my coworkers.

173
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,780
My boss, Chief Ohara.

174
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:02,480
Nice to meet you.

175
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,140
Nice to meet you!

176
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,540
And my senior, Ryo-san.

177
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:09,080
Aloha, aloha.

178
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,080
10 points.

179
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,640
20, 20, 20, 40.

180
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:15,940
What are you talking about?

181
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:16,700
This old guy.

182
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:19,480
The prince's Japanese is

183
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,680
perfectly fluent, you know.

184
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,000
You idiot, why didn't you say that first?

185
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,340
It's me who

186
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:27,460
will become the man who
shoulders Japan's future,

187
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,220
that's the plan, got it?

188
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:36,900
This gorilla's jokes
are really over the line.

189
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:39,040
I got called a piglet,
and I'm not taking that.

190
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,780
What do you mean, piglet?

191
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,960
Now, now, it's a birthday party, after all.

192
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,420
Let's all get along.

193
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:49,900
Once the greetings are over,
I've got no business here.

194
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:51,040
I'm leaving.

195
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:52,340
Hey!

196
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:58,820
Prince, please don't mind him.

197
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:03,760
Don't mess with me, you idiot gorilla!

198
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:14,360
Yoita-san, make ten servings each
of fatty tuna and sea urchin sushi.

199
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:20,600
Sorry, but we were told not to make any sushi
until the prince blows out the candles on his cake.

200
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:24,000
I haven't eaten a thing
since yesterday. Please!

201
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,140
Go on, make some for him.

202
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:26,300
Your Highness.

203
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:28,920
I permit it. Go on, make some.

204
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:31,660
He's a good guy, isn't he?

205
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:36,940
What's going on?

206
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:41,960
He's Keiichi's senior, so I told
them to make him extra-special sushi.

207
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:46,440
You'd make a great king!
Well, hurry up and make the sushi, will you?

208
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:47,060
Hey!

209
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:48,520
Here you go!

210
00:12:49,620 --> 00:13:09,360
Whooooooooo...

211
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,740
Badmouth someone and you'll
get what's coming to you!

212
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:13,380
And now, His Highness

213
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:14,180
will blow out

214
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:15,440
the candles, please.

215
00:13:16,180 --> 00:13:18,700
Please come up to the prince's stage.

216
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:19,900
Okay, okay.

217
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,080
Why does that guy hold a grudge against me?

218
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:41,600
Brats like that need a good smack down.

219
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:57,100
Mm.

220
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:01,540
Eeeeeh?!

221
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:13,300
Whaaaat?!

222
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:15,880
Now!

223
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:23,980
That's a failure!

224
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:34,520
What did you do to the prince?!

225
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:36,060
Just a joke, right?

226
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:39,620
Gorilla, you'd better remember this.

227
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:45,760
Young master, may I have a word with you?

228
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:51,220
What? A suspicious person
has infiltrated this mansion?

229
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:56,420
It seems to be the work of anti-government
elements from the Bookshelf Kingdom.

230
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:57,300
So that means -

231
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:00,140
What's wrong, Nakagawa?

232
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:01,800
Chief, it's terrible!

233
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:04,820
A terrorist has infiltrated
the place to target the prince!

234
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:05,460
What?

235
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:08,820
Alright!

236
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:12,320
Okay, let's start with
the Chinese food first.

237
00:15:14,260 --> 00:15:15,220
This one,

238
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:18,800
and this one,

239
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,940
and then this one too.

240
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:27,160
This one, this one, this one, and this one.

241
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:34,360
This should be enough, right?

242
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,240
Aaaaaah!

243
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,900
Aaaaaah!

244
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:43,180
Serves you right!

245
00:15:43,660 --> 00:15:44,560
Drop dead!

246
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,520
Aaaaaah!

247
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:50,860
I don't even have the energy to run.

248
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:56,260
Aim properly.

249
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:57,220
I know.

250
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:04,900
Come on, let's find the terrorist quickly.

251
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:05,960
Where's Ryo-chan?

252
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:08,160
Even if he's here, he's no help at all.

253
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:11,740
First, we must secure
the safety of the guests.

254
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:12,280
Yeah.

255
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:38,200
!

256
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:38,700
I won!

257
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,600
What's wrong?

258
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:50,920
What happened?

259
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:51,900
Everyone!

260
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:53,660
It's dangerous!

261
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,480
Please stop them!

262
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:57,040
A terrorist has broken into this mansion!

263
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:03,500
My meat...

264
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:06,580
My meat...

265
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:08,960
Meat, nyaa!

266
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,000
Damn it, failed again.

267
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:13,880
If it comes to this,
there's no other choice.

268
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:16,260
We'll storm in, prince and all.

269
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:29,620
What-what's going on?

270
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:35,820
This is...

271
00:17:36,460 --> 00:17:37,700
Please stay calm.

272
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,980
The center of this room
is moving underground.

273
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:42,360
It's all right now.

274
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,060
Whoa! The food!

275
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:47,820
You've got to be kidding me!
I haven't eaten anything yet!

276
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,080
Ryo-chan.

277
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:52,840
Senpai.

278
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,960
Ryo-chan, come down here.

279
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:56,700
Leave that idiot alone.

280
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,740
The terrorist is after the prince!

281
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:00,400
If we just get the prince to safety...

282
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:03,060
Prince

283
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:05,220
Your Highness

284
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,360
This is the worst-case scenario!

285
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,620
Hey, let go of it!

286
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,740
I'm never letting you eat it!

287
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:17,300
Idiot, stop! Hey!

288
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,040
One last one!

289
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,080
Take this!

290
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:34,640
Get back here!

291
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:39,840
Whoa!

292
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:44,080
Senpai! Prince!
Please get out of the room right away!

293
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:46,180
Ugh, this is no time for that!

294
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,240
Whoa!

295
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:04,860
My beloved roast chicken!

296
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:05,840
What!?

297
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:07,980
I found it first, you know!

298
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,560
It's eat or be eaten, you son of a bitch.

299
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,900
Idiot! Is this really the time for that!

300
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,140
Terrorist Makurudo!

301
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:15,640
He's here!

302
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:18,560
Hands up!

303
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:24,400
Dammit! I said this isn't the time for that!

304
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:29,780
You son of a bitch, you did it!

305
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,020
Don't ignore us, damn it!

306
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:39,460
Mariaki's...

307
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:41,520
Mariaki...

308
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:45,860
It's the real deal.

309
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,120
Bastard.

310
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:54,360
It's the real thing.

311
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,320
Where did Mariaki go?

312
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:08,280
What?

313
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:18,160
Time's up.

314
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:19,960
That's enough, don't you think?

315
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:29,260
Alright, you're under arrest!

316
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,380
Roasted whole.

317
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:34,640
Where is he?

318
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:35,620
Mariaki

319
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:35,920
Prince

320
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:37,660
Mariaki

321
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:41,520
Prince, don't you recognize these guys?

322
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:46,980
Chief

323
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:48,160
Too bad.

324
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:49,500
Don't move!

325
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:52,620
Everyone,
drop your guns and raise your hands!

326
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,100
That's the end of it.

327
00:21:04,020 --> 00:21:04,580
Tell me.

328
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:09,160
Prince, it's all right.

329
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,600
If only Senpai would just

330
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,340
flip that switch.

331
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:17,180
Not here, not here,
not here, not here, not here.

332
00:21:17,180 --> 00:21:18,520
Where's the whole roast?

333
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:21,160
Where's my whole roast?

334
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,420
Whole roast, whole roast.

335
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:25,640
Maybe you're looking for
a whole roasted large bird

336
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:26,900
No way.

337
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:28,840
What are you whispering about?

338
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:31,940
Are you chanting a prayer or something?

339
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:34,880
You'll die, just as you wished.

340
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:40,100
Found it! The whole roast!
Thanks for the food!

341
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:54,940
Yes!

342
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:56,100
Senpai!

343
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:58,280
W-what happened?

344
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:58,820
We did it!

345
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:01,740
Senpai turned on the trapdoor switch for us.

346
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:06,660
The roast! The roast went that way!

347
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:10,740
Found it!

348
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:12,460
Found it!

349
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:16,920
Well done, Ryo-chan. You're a sly one.

350
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:19,180
Thanks to you, senpai, I was saved.

351
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,000
Thanks, Ryo-san.

352
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:24,940
W-well, that's about all there is to it.

353
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:29,840
What's this?

354
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:32,240
That's...

355
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:37,740
Throw it all away.

356
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:53,720
Looks like someone pressed it.

357
00:22:53,720 --> 00:22:54,940
Aaaah!

358
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:01,080
Here, it's the Katsushika
Station Chief Award.

359
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:02,980
Yo! Well done, you did good.

360
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,040
I don't want that kind of thing.

361
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:08,396
Aaaah, the roast...

362
00:23:08,446 --> 00:23:11,340
I want sushi! I want the feast!

363
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:15,760
Not being able to eat the party
food must have really shocked you.

364
00:23:16,460 --> 00:23:17,680
Here you go, sorry to keep you waiting.

365
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:20,580
What about you?

366
00:23:20,580 --> 00:23:22,860
Thanks for saving me. Seriously,

367
00:23:22,910 --> 00:23:26,240
Last night was a lot of fun.
Eat me, won't you?

368
00:23:26,420 --> 00:23:27,640
The prince!

369
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:34,120
Aren't you thoughtful.

370
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:41,700
Wasabi!

371
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:47,160
He fell for it again. What an idiot, really.

372
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:48,180
You brat!

373
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:08,180
Hand-knitting is fine! This Kankichi Ryotsu is an Edokko,
and that's that!

374
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:10,920
Edokko have a weakness for fires,
fights, and sushi!

375
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:14,960
You expect an Edokko to get into a lukewarm bath like this?
Make it hotter!

376
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:17,840
It's not hot at all!

377
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:21,200
Next time: the clash of the Edokko battle!
See you then!

378
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:36,640
Let's always keep smiling, okay?

379
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:40,860
Even when something outrageous happens,

380
00:24:40,860 --> 00:24:45,360
keep smiling sweetly, okay?

381
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:50,560
Just head out with a
face like nothing's wrong.

382
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:57,420
Hey, smile for me. It's not your fault.

383
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:05,720
Hey, smile for me,
like you were a moment ago.

384
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:16,600
Keep smiling always, because a woman who
shakes off the jet-black night isn't beautiful.

385
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:21,320
You should smile right away.

386
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:25,800
Unless you're a child, that is.

